# Template for .env.bot — the Telegram control bot.
#   cp .env.bot.example .env.bot && chmod 600 .env.bot
# The real file is gitignored; this template is tracked. No values here, ever.

# --- the bot itself --------------------------------------------------------
# Create the bot by messaging @BotFather on Telegram: /newbot, pick a name and
# a username. It replies with the token.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Numeric chat ids allowed to drive the bot. Space or comma separated.
# This is the only thing standing between your Deluge and anyone who guesses
# the bot's username, so it is not optional — the bot refuses to start empty.
# Find yours: fill in the token above, message your bot, then run
#   python -m server.chat_id
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_CHAT_IDS=

# --- guard rails -----------------------------------------------------------
# Requests per day before the bot refuses, counted across restarts. Counts
# attempts rather than successes: a failed run still cost tokens.
TELEGRAM_DAILY_LIMIT=20

# Which agent config the bot drives. Leave unset for config.toml (the native
# stack); set to config.rehearsal.toml for the containerised one.
TORRENT_AGENT_CONFIG=

# --- the agent's own key ---------------------------------------------------
# A daemon cannot rely on the interactive-shell guard in ~/.bashrc that the CLI
# depends on, so the key has to reach the bot one of two ways:
#
#   a) launch through an interactive shell, which sources ~/.bashrc for you:
#        bash -ic 'set -a; . .env.bot; set +a; .venv/bin/python -m server.bot'
#   b) set it here, and launch however you like.
#
# LEAVE THE LINE COMMENTED OUT IF YOU USE (a). Sourcing this file with a bare
# `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=` assigns an EMPTY string over the one ~/.bashrc just
# exported. /help and /status still work, so the bot looks healthy — only /get
# fails, with an auth error that points at Anthropic rather than at this file.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- ai-data-store (optional) -----------------------------------------------
# The unattended layer (this bot, and the autodeliver pipeline) cannot use the
# Claude Code PostToolUse hook that normally logs to ai-data-store — it isn't
# a Claude Code session. torrent_agent/ai_data_store.py posts directly
# instead, using its own credential rather than ~/.claude.json.
#
# Copy the values from ~/.claude.json's mcpServers.ai-data-store entry (url,
# and the token after "Bearer " in headers.Authorization).
#
# PUT THESE HERE ONLY — NEVER IN .env. .env is what the interactive
# Claude-Code-skill path sources; setting them there double-posts every
# interactive /get (once via the hook, once via this module).
#AI_DATA_STORE_URL=
#AI_DATA_STORE_TOKEN=
